er with no other-family seat (the new test covers it). One gap remains: `answers[-1]` is the latest answer, not necessarily the one round 1 ruled on. An answer appended after the REROLL that does not cover the fix head would be the one checked. The code comment (\"which round 1 ruled on\") states more than the code does. Low stakes: either answer is a real gaze answer of this review.\n\nChecks:\n- touched-tests: selected: tests/test_attribution_notes.py tests/test_attribution_seats.py tests/test_forge_offline.py tests/test_gaze_branch.py tests/test_gaze_close.py tests/test_gaze_intent.py tests/test_gaze_seat.py tests/test_gaze_setup.py tests/test_gaze_wall_endpoints.py tests/test_raid_land.py tests/test_raid_land_local.py tests/test_raid_noforge_f2.py tests/test_review_notes.py tests/test_review_notes_gate.py tests/test_seat_clock.py; fallback: none; result: pass (15 selected file(s)), 371 passed.\n- Verified as fixed: a self or subagent seat labelled with another family no longer counts (test_self_and_subagent_seats_never_count_as_cross_family). gaze_seat.py checks the stamped family against the door and the provider, so the header family really is set by the launcher.\n\nunresolved_review_comments: []\nunresolved_simplify_findings: []\n"}

